<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="global_bond_rout::bond_market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Expanded, tightly enforced sanctions against banks, asset custodians or commodity-linked counterparties disrupt cross-border settlement and repo/interdealer activity, reducing depth and widening bid-ask spreads in global bond markets.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rout</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="global_fuel_supply_shock::export_control_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Expanded and enforced sanction regimes impose formal bans, secondary restrictions and shipping/insurance constraints that increase aggregate export controls on crude and refined shipments.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_fuel_supply_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="global_fuel_supply_shock::refined_inventory_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Sanctions and related trade restrictions block or deter imports of Russian refined products to dependent markets, directly reducing available refined‑fuel inventories there.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">global_fuel_supply_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="hormuz_redsea_tensions::global_oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter and more effectively enforced sanctions reduce Russian export volumes and raise shipping/insurance frictions, directly tightening available crude supply and pushing benchmark prices upward.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">hormuz_redsea_tensions</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="indo_pacific_rivalry::financing_constraints" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Expansion and enforcement of secondary sanctions and compliance controls tied to the Russia war prompt global banks and insurers to de-risk, withdraw correspondent services, and add sanction-related covenants, directly raising the cost and availability barriers for financing strategic Indo‑Pacific infrastructure projects.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">indo_pacific_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::sanctions_pressure" target="indo_pacific_rivalry::strategic_investment_flo" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Heightened sanctions risk increases due‑diligence and counterparty concerns among institutional investors and state-backed financiers, causing a measurable diversion or postponement of cross‑border strategic capital flows into projects in the Indo‑Pacific that involve counterparties exposed to secondary sanctions.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">indo_pacific_rivalry</data>
</edge>
