<edge source="hormuz_redsea_tensions::chokepoint_throughput" target="global_bond_rout::long_benchmark_yield" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained reductions in throughput through major chokepoints raise expected near-term inflation and term premia as markets price persistent supply constraints, putting upward pressure on long-dated sovereign yields.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">hormuz_redsea_tensions</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rout</data>
</edge>
<edge source="hormuz_redsea_tensions::chokepoint_throughput" target="global_fuel_supply_shock::refined_inventory_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">A fall in chokepoint throughput immediately reduces crude and refined product arrivals to refineries and terminals, lowering on‑hand refined fuel stocks as deliveries and refinery outputs drop.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">hormuz_redsea_tensions</data>
  <data key="d39">global_fuel_supply_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="hormuz_redsea_tensions::chokepoint_throughput" target="indo_pacific_rivalry::strategic_investment_flo" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher uninterrupted throughput reduces the perceived urgency to diversify routes and build alternative terminals or stocks, thereby lowering the volume of strategic infrastructure and energy investment flowing into the Indo‑Pacific.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">hormuz_redsea_tensions</data>
  <data key="d39">indo_pacific_rivalry</data>
</edge>
