<edge source="global_bond_rout::long_benchmark_yield" target="global_fuel_supply_shock::fuel_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher long-term benchmark yields raise borrowing and inventory-financing costs for oil producers, refiners and traders, which they pass through to wholesale/pump fuel prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_rout</data>
  <data key="d39">global_fuel_supply_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rout::long_benchmark_yield" target="hormuz_redsea_tensions::global_oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in long-term benchmark yields attracts capital into the currency of that sovereign bond (e.g., USD), appreciating it and making dollar-priced crude more expensive for other currencies, reducing demand and putting downward pressure on global oil prices within weeks.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_rout</data>
  <data key="d39">hormuz_redsea_tensions</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rout::long_benchmark_yield" target="indo_pacific_rivalry::financing_constraints" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.9</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising long-term benchmark yields directly raise the cost of borrowing and debt-service for sovereigns and project sponsors, making capital for large infrastructure and energy projects more expensive or conditional and therefore tightening financing availability in the Indo‑Pacific.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_rout</data>
  <data key="d39">indo_pacific_rivalry</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_bond_rout::long_benchmark_yield" target="russia_ukraine_war::defense_funding" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in long-term sovereign yields raises governments' debt-service and borrowing costs, compressing fiscal space and prompting delays or downscaling of new defense commitments and disbursements for Ukraine support.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_bond_rout</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
