<edge source="indo_pacific_rivalry::alliance_commitment_stoc" target="hormuz_redsea_tensions::military_deploy_intensit" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Stronger alliance commitments and force-posture emphasis in the Indo‑Pacific require redeployment of limited US and partner naval and air assets to that theater, reducing sustained force presence and operations available for Hormuz/Red Sea corridors.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">indo_pacific_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">hormuz_redsea_tensions</data>
</edge>
<edge source="indo_pacific_rivalry::alliance_commitment_stoc" target="russia_ukraine_war::alliance_cohesion" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">If major powers (principally the US) deepen and clarify security commitments toward Indo‑Pacific partners, political and burden‑sharing tensions will rise among Euro‑Atlantic partners as they disagree over prioritization, reducing coordinated political and military alignment on Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">indo_pacific_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
