<edge source="indo_pacific_rivalry::financing_constraints" target="global_bond_rout::bank_funding_stress" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter availability and cost of project and infrastructure finance forces banks to extend liquidity support, mark loans and absorb delayed cashflows on sponsored projects, degrading balance-sheet liquidity and elevating funding strain.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">indo_pacific_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">global_bond_rout</data>
</edge>
<edge source="indo_pacific_rivalry::financing_constraints" target="global_fuel_supply_shock::market_supply_expectatio" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter financing for imports, shipping, and refining reduces traders' and refiners' ability to procure and carry product, causing market participants to revise expectations toward tighter future supply.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">indo_pacific_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">global_fuel_supply_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="indo_pacific_rivalry::financing_constraints" target="russia_ukraine_war::defense_funding" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.55</data>
  <data key="d36">Tighter, more expensive capital conditions in the Indo‑Pacific reduce governments' and export/credit agencies' ability to finance large overseas expenditures, leading to lower available budgets and loan guarantees that could have been redirected as defense aid or procurement for Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">indo_pacific_rivalry</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
